He is often credited with inventing many other cocktails,<ref name="fieldguide" /> including the [[Bloody Mary (cocktail)|Bloody Mary]], the [[Sidecar (cocktail)|Sidecar]], the [[Monkey Gland]],<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.esquire.com/drinks/white-lady-drink-recipe|first=David|last=Wondrich|publisher=Esquire.com|title=White Lady|date=5 November 2007}}</ref> the [[Paradise (cocktail)|Paradise]], the [[Boulevardier (cocktail)|Boulevardier]],<ref>{{cite news |date=2 February 2012| url=http://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/02/02/case-study-the-boulevardier/ |title=Case Study: The Boulevardier |work= The New York Times |accessdate=7 November 2015 |first=Toby|last=Cecchini}}</ref> and an early form of the [[French 75 (cocktail)|French 75]].

